      "name": "IsLibraryInitialized",
      "signature": "bool IsLibraryInitialized(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Check if the library has completed initialization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load the global initialization state variable (g_bLibraryInitialized)\n2. Compare the value against the completion sentinel (0x2)\n3. Return true if initialization is complete, false otherwise\n\nReturns:\n- true: Library initialization is complete (g_bLibraryInitialized == 2)\n- false: Library initialization has not completed or failed\n\nPurpose:\nThis function serves as a fast query to determine if the library has successfully\ncompleted its initialization sequence. It is typically called by other components\nbefore using library functionality to ensure the library is ready.\n\nNote:\nThe initialization state is tracked via the global variable g_bLibraryInitialized\nwhich uses value 0x2 as the completion sentinel. This is more specific than a\nsimple boolean flag, allowing for multiple initialization states (0=uninitialized,\n1=initializing, 2=complete).",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
