      "name": "InitializeClientSocket",
      "signature": "BOOL InitializeClientSocket(char * szHostname)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "BOOL",
      "comment": "InitializeClientSocket - Initializes Winsock and establishes a TCP socket connection to a server.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize Winsock with WSAStartup (version 1.1)\n2. Create a TCP stream socket (AF_INET, SOCK_STREAM)\n3. Configure sockaddr structure with port 4000\n4. Resolve hostname to IP address\n5. Connect socket to the server\n\nParameters:\n  szHostname - Server hostname or IP address to connect to\n\nReturns: TRUE (always returns 1, sets g_hClientSocket to 0 on connect failure)",
