      "name": "NET_GetPacketSize",
      "signature": "uint NET_GetPacketSize(byte * pbPacketData, uint dwBufferSize, uint * pdwOutPacketSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Parses network packet header to determine total packet size.\n\nClassification: Worker function - packet size calculation for network parsing\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Return 0 if buffer is empty (dwBufferSize == 0)\n2. Read packet type byte from pbPacketData[0]\n3. Return 0 if packet type > 0xAC (invalid range)\n4. Look up base size from g_adwPacketSizeLookup[packetType]\n5. Store lookup value in *pdwOutPacketSize\n6. If lookup value is 0, return 0 (unknown packet type)\n7. If lookup value > 0 (fixed size), return lookup value\n8. If lookup value < 0 (variable size), use switch on packet type:\n   - 0x16: Require 13 bytes min, size = word at offset 1\n   - 0x26: Require 10 bytes min, size = 12 + strlen(str1) + strlen(str2)\n   - 0x5B: Require 34 bytes min, size = word at offset 1\n   - 0x94: Require 9 bytes min, size = (byte[1] + 2) * 3\n   - 0x9C: Require 3 bytes min, size = byte at offset 2\n   - 0x9D: Require 3 bytes min, size = byte at offset 2\n   - 0xA6: Require 4 bytes min, size = word at offset 2\n   - 0xA7: Require 2 bytes min, size = byte[1] + 1 (or 2 if byte[1] == 0)\n   - 0xAB: Require 8 bytes min, size = byte[1] + 7\n   - default: Set size to 0\n9. Return calculated packet size\n\nParameters:\n  pbPacketData     - byte * - ECX - Pointer to packet data buffer\n  dwBufferSize     - uint   - EDX - Available bytes in buffer\n  pdwOutPacketSize - uint * - Stack - Output: calculated packet size\n\nReturns:\n  Packet size on success (also stored in *pdwOutPacketSize)\n  0 on failure (insufficient data, invalid type, or unknown packet)\n\nVariable-Length Packet Types:\n  Type  Min   Size Calculation\n  0x16  13    Word at offset 1 (chat message with length prefix)\n  0x26  10    Fixed header + two null-terminated strings\n  0x5B  34    Word at offset 1 (large data packet)\n  0x94  9     (count + 2) * 3 (array of 3-byte entries)\n  0x9C  3     Byte at offset 2 (small variable packet)\n  0x9D  3     Byte at offset 2 (small variable packet)\n  0xA6  4     Word at offset 2 (medium variable packet)\n  0xA7  2     Compression control (1 or byte[1]+1)\n  0xAB  8     Byte[1] + 7 (extended header packet)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xAC - Maximum valid packet type\n  0x0D (13) - Minimum size for type 0x16\n  0x0A (10) - Minimum size for type 0x26\n  0x22 (34) - Minimum size for type 0x5B\n  0x09 (9) - Minimum size for type 0x94\n\nRelated Globals:\n  g_adwPacketSizeLookup - Packet type to base size lookup table (173 entries)\n  g_abPacketSwitchIndex - Jump table index for variable-size types\n  g_adwPacketSwitchJumpTable - Switch statement jump addresses\n\nCalled By:\n  NET_ParseAndQueuePackets - Main packet parsing loop\n  NET_QueuePacketForShutdown - Shutdown packet queuing",
