      "name": "ValidateAndProcessQueuedMessage",
      "signature": "bool ValidateAndProcessQueuedMessage(void * this, undefined4 queuedMessage)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Validates queued message size and processes it if valid.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compare message size (in AX) against maximum threshold of 0x204 (516 bytes)\n2. If size exceeds threshold, retrieve return address via GetReturnAddress(0x20e)\n3. Call CleanupAndAbort with error context and return address\n4. Call _exit(-1) to terminate program (no return from failure path)\n5. If size valid: load queued message pointer from global [0x02c6b424]\n6. Call ProcessQueuedMessage with message data, size, and parameters\n7. Convert result to boolean using NEG/SBB pattern\n8. Return success status in EAX\n\nParameters:\n  queuedMessage: Queued message data or context pointer (passed on stack)\n\nReturns:\n  bool: TRUE if message processed successfully, FALSE if processing failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Size validation against 0x204 (516): Prevents buffer overflow in processing\n  On validation failure: Calls CleanupAndAbort and _exit(-1) - function never returns\n  NEG/SBB pattern: Converts non-zero result (success) to TRUE, zero to FALSE",
