      "name": "ValidateAndProcessNetworkPacket",
      "signature": "int ValidateAndProcessNetworkPacket(void * this, byte * pPacketData, uint nBufferSize, uint * pPacketSize, uint * pReserved, int * pPacketType, uint * pPriority, int param8)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Validates and processes incoming network packets with size and type checking.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check buffer size parameter is non-zero (minimum 1 byte), return 3 if invalid\n2. Load packet type code from first byte of packet data\n3. Call CalculatePacketSize to parse packet and get actual payload size\n4. Validate parse result is non-zero (parsing succeeded)\n5. Validate packet type code is in acceptable range (0x67-0x70 or 0xff)\n6. Validate parsed packet size does not exceed maximum of 0x204 (516 bytes)\n7. Validate packet fits within provided buffer (parsed size <= buffer size)\n8. Set reserved output parameter to 0\n9. Return parsed packet size to caller via output parameter\n10. Calculate packet priority/type value: 1 if type < 0x67, 2 if type >= 0x71, 0 otherwise\n11. Set priority output parameter to 100\n12. Return status code based on calculated type value: 2 if type=0, 1 if type=1, 2 if type=2\n\nParameters:\n  pPacketData (ECX): Pointer to network packet buffer (starts with type byte)\n  nBufferSize (EDX): Size of provided buffer in bytes\n  pPacketSize (stack): Output pointer to receive parsed packet size\n  pReserved (stack): Output pointer, set to 0\n  pPacketType (stack): Output pointer to receive packet type/priority value\n  pPriority (stack): Output pointer, set to 100 (constant priority)\n\nReturns:\n  1: Success, packet type = 1\n  2: Success, packet type = 0 or packet type = 2\n  3: Error, invalid buffer size (0 bytes) or packet too large for buffer\n  4: Error, invalid packet type code (not 0x67-0x70 and not 0xff)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Packet types 0x67-0x70 and 0xff are accepted, others rejected\n  - Type 0x67-0x66 sets priority 1, type >= 0x71 sets priority 2, others 0\n  - Returns different codes (1,2) based on type to signal packet handling priority\n  - Maximum packet size limited to 516 bytes (0x204)",
