      "name": "SendInitializationMessage",
      "signature": "uint SendInitializationMessage(void * this, uint contextHandle, uint sessionData)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Callback handler that sends an initialization message during game session setup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 2-byte local buffer on stack\n2. Construct message payload with magic bytes 0xAF (resource type) and 0x01 (version)\n3. Call external write function with null terminator, session data, message buffer, and length 2\n4. Return success status (1)\n\nParameters:\n  contextHandle (uint): Game context handle passed by session initializer\n  sessionData (uint): Session-specific data forwarded to external write function\n\nReturns:\n  uint: Always returns 1 (success status)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Magic Numbers: 0xAF is the message type identifier for initialization\n                0x01 is the protocol version\n                2 is the fixed message length in bytes\n  Role: This is handler slot 2 in the four-handler initialization callback sequence\n        Called by InitializeGameSession after loading context parameters",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
