      "name": "InitializeAllModules",
      "signature": "int InitializeAllModules(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes all modules in the module chain under critical section protection.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Enter critical section with validation to ensure thread-safe access\n2. Load current node pointer from module list head (via implicit ESI register)\n3. While current node is not null:\n   a. Load next node pointer from current node offset +0x20c\n   b. Call InitializeModule(0x5d, 0) to initialize current module\n   c. Advance to next node in chain\n4. Exit critical section\n5. Return success status (1)\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT ESI: Pointer to module list head (linked list of modules)\nIMPLICIT EDI: Pointer to critical section object\nIMPLICIT EDX: Module initialization code (0x57 - set before call)\n\nReturns:\nEAX: Success status (1 = success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty module list: Loop exits immediately if first node is null\n- Module chain traversal: Uses linked list with next pointer at offset +0x20c\n- InitializeModule call: Always passes constant 0x5d as module ID and 0 as parameter\n- Critical section: Protects entire initialization sequence against concurrent access\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x5d (93): Module initialization constant passed to InitializeModule\n0x20c (524): Offset to next pointer in module node structure\n\nStructure Layout:\nModule node structure (accessed via ESI and offsets):\nOffset | Size | Field      | Type    | Description\n0x000  | 4    | (data)     | void*   | Module data at current offset\n0x20c  | 4    | next       | void*   | Pointer to next module in chain",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
