      "name": "ProcessIncomingPackets",
      "signature": "int ProcessIncomingPackets(int param1)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Process incoming network packets and queue them for handling\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate buffer size is positive\n2. Loop while data remains in buffer:\n   a. Allocate 0x1fc byte packet buffer via AllocateMemoryWithTracking\n   b. Read packet data from input buffer via ExtractPacketFieldValue\n   c. Validate packet size (must be 1-516 bytes)\n   d. Copy packet data to allocated buffer\n   e. Store packet size at offset +0x204\n   f. Store timestamp at offset +0x208 via GetTickCount\n   g. Clear next pointer at offset +0x20c\n   h. Route packet based on type byte to appropriate queue\n   i. Update global queue pointers (g_pHighPriorityQueue/g_pNormalQueue)\n   j. Advance input buffer pointer by bytesRead\n3. Return when all data processed\n\nParameters:\n  this - Context object pointer (passed via ECX in __thiscall)\n  pInBuffer - Pointer to incoming network data buffer\n  bufferSize - Total bytes available in input buffer\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Packet size > 0x204 (516): Fatal error 0x202\n  - Packet size <= 0: Fatal error 0x203  \n  - Packet type > 0xB4: Fatal error 0x216 or 0x21d\n  - Error handler calls GetReturnAddress, CleanupAndAbort, then _exit(-1)\n  - Queue pointers: DAT_02c6b3fc (high priority), DAT_02c6b3f4 (normal)\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field        Type    Description\n------  ----  -----------  ------  -----------\n0x000   508   data         byte[]  Packet payload data\n0x204   4     dataSize     uint    Actual bytes in packet\n0x208   4     timestamp    DWORD   GetTickCount timestamp \n0x20c   4     pNext        ptr     Next packet in queue\n\nNote: Function uses 2 stack-allocated temporary variables (local_10c, local_110) optimized away by decompiler",
