      "name": "InitializeNetworkConnection",
      "signature": "int InitializeNetworkConnection(int param1)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes network connection by setting up Winsock, creating a socket, and connecting to remote server on port 4000\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize Windows Sockets with WSAStartup(0x101, &WSADATA)\n2. Create TCP socket using socket(AF_INET=2, SOCK_STREAM=1, 0)\n3. Check for socket creation error; if EAX == -1, call WSAGetLastError() and skip initialization\n4. Initialize sockaddr_in structure at DAT_02c6b24c with address family AF_INET (0x2)\n5. Set port to network byte order using htons(0xfa0=4000)\n6. Call ResolveNetworkAddress() to get host address string\n7. Convert hostname to IP address using inet_addr()\n8. Attempt TCP connection using connect(socket, &sockaddr_in, 0x10)\n9. If connect failed (result == -1), clear socket handle to 0\n10. Return 1 (success status code)\n\nStructure Layout:\nsockaddr_in at DAT_02c6b24c (16 bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field Name        Type    Description\n  0x0     2     sin_family        word    Address family (0x2 = AF_INET)\n  0x2     2     sin_port          word    Port in network byte order (htons result)\n  0x4     4     sin_addr          uint    IP address from inet_addr()\n  0x8     8     sin_zero          byte[8] Padding (zeros)\n\nReturn Value: 1 (always returns success regardless of connection result)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
