      "name": "SetThreadInitializationMode",
      "signature": "void SetThreadInitializationMode(void * this, int nMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Set thread initialization mode if library not yet initialized\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load g_bLibraryInitialized from 0x02c6b418 into EAX\n2. Check if g_bLibraryInitialized == 1 (fully initialized state)\n3. If initialized, jump to already_initialized_exit and return\n4. Check if g_bLibraryInitialized == 2 (alternate initialization state)\n5. If in alternate state, jump to already_initialized_exit and return\n6. Enter critical section at 0x02c6b400 via Ordinal_10050 (EnterCriticalSection)\n7. Load nMode parameter from stack [ESP+4] into EAX\n8. Store nMode to global variable g_nThreadInitMode at 0x02c6b420\n9. Prepare critical section address 0x02c6b400 on stack for LeaveCriticalSection\n10. Exit critical section via indirect jump to LeaveCriticalSection at [0x02c6817c]\n\nParameters:\n  nMode (int) - Thread initialization mode flag to store in g_nThreadInitMode\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Function only modifies g_nThreadInitMode when g_bLibraryInitialized is neither 1 nor 2\n  - Uses critical section synchronization to protect g_nThreadInitMode writes\n  - Tail-call optimization: indirect JMP to LeaveCriticalSection instead of CALL+RET\n  - Called by Ordinal_10019 with nMode=1 during worker thread creation\n  - Critical section object at 0x02c6b400, size varies by OS\n  - Thread mode stored at 0x02c6b420 (4-byte DWORD)\n\nGlobal Variables:\n  g_bLibraryInitialized @ 0x02c6b418 - Library initialization state (1=initialized, 2=alternate)\n  g_nThreadInitMode @ 0x02c6b420 - Thread initialization mode flag\n  CRITICAL_SECTION @ 0x02c6b400 - Synchronization object for thread-safe access",
