      "name": "ResetThreadInitModeIfNeeded",
      "signature": "void ResetThreadInitModeIfNeeded(void * this)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Conditional thread initialization mode reset based on library state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load library initialization state from g_bLibraryInitialized\n2. Check if library is NOT in state 1 (fully initialized)\n3. Check if library is NOT in state 2 (alternate initialized)\n4. If either check passes, proceed to reset:\n   a. Enter critical section for thread-safe access\n   b. Reset g_nThreadInitMode to 0\n   c. Leave critical section\n5. Return to caller\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If g_bLibraryInitialized is 1 or 2, function performs no operation\n- Critical section protects concurrent access to g_nThreadInitMode\n- EDX=0x41 and ECX=0x2c6b400 passed to EnterCriticalSectionWithValidation (implementation detail)\n\nData Accessed:\n- g_bLibraryInitialized (0x02c6b418) - dword flag for library init state\n- g_nThreadInitMode (0x02c6b420) - dword thread mode counter\n- g_CriticalSection (0x02c6b400) - CRITICAL_SECTION object for synchronization",
