      "name": "InitializeThreadMode",
      "signature": "void InitializeThreadMode(void * this)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes thread mode for the library if not already initialized.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear last socket error by calling WSAGetLastError\n2. Load library initialization state from g_bLibraryInitialized\n3. Check if library is already initialized (value 1 or 2)\n4. If already initialized, jump to exit\n5. Enter critical section for thread-safe access\n6. Set g_nThreadInitMode to 0 (reset thread mode)\n7. Leave critical section and return\n\nPurpose: Ensures thread mode is initialized only once per library lifecycle, with synchronization to prevent race conditions during initialization.\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If g_bLibraryInitialized is 1 or 2, the initialization is skipped (library already initialized)\n- Uses critical section locking to prevent concurrent initialization\n- Sets g_nThreadInitMode = 0 as the initialization value",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
