      "name": "CreateMainGameThread",
      "signature": "HANDLE CreateMainGameThread(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Creates a new thread that runs the main game loop.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Receives thread parameter in EAX register (implicit parameter)\n2. Calls CreateThread Windows API with thread procedure InitializeNetworkConnection\n3. Passes the EAX parameter as lpParameter argument to the thread\n4. Sets lpSecurityAttributes to NULL (no security descriptor)\n5. Sets dwStackSize to 0 (default stack size)\n6. Sets dwCreationFlags to 0 (thread runs immediately)\n7. Stores returned thread HANDLE in global variable DAT_02c6b3f8\n8. Stores thread ID in global variable DAT_02c6b240\n9. Returns the thread HANDLE to caller\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT pThreadParam (via EAX): void* - Pointer to thread initialization parameter, passed to thread procedure\n\nReturns:\nHANDLE: Windows thread handle for the created thread, NULL on failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Thread handle stored in global DAT_02c6b3f8 for later access\n- Thread ID stored in global DAT_02c6b240 for identification  \n- No error checking; caller must validate return value\n- Uses __stdcall calling convention but receives implicit parameter via EAX register\n- Thread procedure InitializeNetworkConnection will receive pThreadParam as its lpParameter\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x0 - NULL security attributes (inherit from parent process)\n0x0 - Default stack size (1MB for executables)\n0x0 - Thread starts immediately (not suspended)",
