      "name": "SendSocketData",
      "signature": "int SendSocketData(char * pBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Send data buffer over network socket\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call send() with global socket handle, buffer pointer, and length\n2. If send returns -1 (SOCKET_ERROR), handle error condition\n3. Call WSAGetLastError() to retrieve error code\n4. Check library initialization state (g_bLibraryInitialized)\n5. If not initialized (value != 1 and != 2), perform cleanup\n6. Call Ordinal_10050() cleanup function\n7. Set g_nThreadInitMode to 0\n8. Release critical section lock\n9. Return 0 on error, or number of bytes sent on success\n\nParameters:\n  pBuffer (ECX) - Pointer to data buffer to transmit\n  bufferLength (IMPLICIT EAX) - Number of bytes to send from buffer\n\nReturns:\n  Number of bytes successfully sent, or 0 if send failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Uses global socket handle from DAT_02c6b248\n  - SOCKET_ERROR constant is -1 (0xFFFFFFFF)\n  - Library initialization values: 1 or 2 indicate initialized state\n  - Non-standard calling convention: ECX=buffer, EAX=length (implicit)",
