      "name": "DispatchGameMessage",
      "signature": "int DispatchGameMessage(void * this, void * pGameContext, int messageId)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Dispatches a game message through the message queue system.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load game context/message manager pointer from global data (0x02c6b424)\n2. Allocate and initialize a 20-byte message buffer on the stack\n3. Set message type field (offset +0x13) to 0x70\n4. Call ProcessQueuedMessage to enqueue the message for processing\n5. Return success code (1)\n\nParameters:\n  this (ECX): Pointer to the calling object instance (__thiscall convention)\n  pGameContext (stack): Pointer to game context or message manager instance\n  messageId (stack): Message ID or event type to dispatch\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Message successfully queued and dispatched\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Message type 0x70 (112 decimal) is hardcoded for this message class\n  - Message buffer is stack-allocated and copied by ProcessQueuedMessage\n  - Function always returns success (1) regardless of processing outcome\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0x70 (112): Message type identifier for game dispatch messages\n  0x02c6b424: Global pointer to message manager instance\n  20: Size of message buffer allocated on stack",
