      "name": "__amsg_exit",
      "signature": "void __amsg_exit(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Handles runtime error exit with optional message banner display.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check global runtime display flags (banner and error message)\n2. If banner display enabled (0x02c6adf4 == 1) OR (banner disabled AND error display enabled)\n3. Call __FF_MSGBANNER to display message banner with context parameter\n4. Call DisplayRuntimeError with context parameter to show error message  \n5. Call __exit function pointer with exit code 0xff (255)\n6. Function does not return (noreturn)\n\nParameters:\nIMPLICIT in_ECX (void*): Context parameter passed through to banner and error display functions\nIMPLICIT in_stack_00000004 (uint): Exit code parameter passed to __exit function\n\nReturns:\nThis function does not return (noreturn). Program execution terminates.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Banner display controlled by global flags at 0x02c6adf4 and 0x02c6adf8\n- Exit code 0xff indicates abnormal termination\n- Context parameter may be NULL\n\nGlobal References:\n0x02c6adf4 - Banner display flag (1 = enabled)  \n0x02c6adf8 - Error message display flag (1 = enabled)\n0x02c6a030 - Function pointer to __exit routine\n\nError Handling:\nNo error handling - function terminates program execution in all cases.",
