      "name": "ReportSecurityFailure",
      "signature": "void ReportSecurityFailure(void * this, int nFailureType)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "comment": "Reports security failures and terminates the process with detailed error information.\n\nAlgorithm:\n\n1. Initialize stack security cookie by XORing __security_cookie with EBP\n2. Check if custom security failure handler is registered at global DAT_02c6b16c\n3. If no custom handler registered:\n   a. Determine failure type: buffer overrun (type 1) or unknown security failure\n   b. Set appropriate error message string based on failure type\n   c. Get current module filename using GetModuleFileNameA with 260-character buffer\n   d. If GetModuleFileNameA fails, use placeholder \"<program_name_unknown>\" string\n   e. Check if filename length + 11 characters exceeds 60 characters\n   f. If too long, truncate filename and prepend \"...\" ellipsis prefix\n   g. Allocate stack buffer for complete error message\n   h. Build formatted message: error title + newlines + \"Program: \" + filename + detailed description\n   i. Display error message using ___crtMessageBoxA with flags 0x12010\n4. If custom handler is registered:\n   a. Clear exception list pointer\n   b. Call custom handler function via function pointer\n   c. Reset exception list to 0xffffffff\n5. Terminate process with exit code 3 (security failure)\n6. Execute software interrupt 3 and call exception handler\n\nParameters:\n\nfailureType (int): Type of security failure detected\n  1 = Buffer overrun detected\n  Other values = Unknown security failure\n\nIMPLICIT:\nthis (void*): Object instance pointer (unused in implementation)\n\nReturns:\n\nvoid: Function never returns - always terminates process\n\nSpecial Cases:\n\nBuffer Overrun (failureType == 1): Uses specific \"Buffer overrun detected!\" message\nUnknown Security Failure: Uses generic \"Unknown security failure detected\" message\nLong Filename Handling: Filenames longer than 49 characters are truncated with \"...\" prefix\nGetModuleFileNameA Failure: Falls back to \"<program_name_unknown>\" placeholder\nCustom Handler Mode: Bypasses built-in MessageBox and calls registered function pointer\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n\n0x104 (260): Maximum path length for GetModuleFileNameA buffer including null terminator\n0x3c (60): Maximum total message length before truncating filename\n0xb (11): Additional characters added to filename (\"Program: \" prefix)\n3: Exit code for security failure termination\n0x12010: MessageBox flags (MB_ICONHAND | MB_SETFOREGROUND | MB_TASKMODAL)\n0x02c6b16c: Global address storing custom security failure handler function pointer\n\nError Handling:\n\nGetModuleFileNameA failure: Returns to placeholder program name\nLong filename: Automatic truncation with ellipsis prefix\nStack overflow protection: Security cookie validation prevents stack corruption\nProcess termination: Always exits with code 3, no error recovery possible\n\nStructure Layout:\n\nStack Frame Security:\nOffset  Size  Field Name                Type        Description\n+0      4     pExceptionList           void*       SEH exception list pointer  \n+4      4     returnAddress            uint        Return address for SEH\n+8      4     cookieXor                uint        XOR'd security cookie value\n+12     1     nullByte                 byte        Null terminator byte\n+16     260   moduleFileName           char[260]   Module filename buffer\n+276    4     pMessageBuffer           byte*       Pointer to message buffer\n+280    4     pFailureTypeString       char*       Error message string pointer",
