      "name": "ShutdownResourceManager",
      "signature": "void ShutdownResourceManager(void * this)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "comment": "Shutdown and cleanup the global resource manager instance.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load the global resource manager handle from 0x02c6b424\n2. Prepare cleanup parameters: manager handle, status buffer address, and cleanup flag (1)\n3. Call DestroyResourceManager via indirect dispatch to perform cleanup\n4. Clear the global resource manager pointer to null (0x00000000)\n5. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone - operates on global state only\n\nReturns:\nvoid - no return value, function performs cleanup as side effect\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic value 0xB0 (176) is written to status buffer before cleanup call\n- Global pointer is unconditionally cleared after call, preventing reuse\n- Used during engine shutdown or context cleanup sequence\n- Ordinal 10028 from original DLL export table\n\nStructure Layout:\nGlobal Resource Manager Pointer (0x02c6b424):\n- Stores address of active resource manager instance\n- Set to null after cleanup to invalidate all references\n- Accessed as read at 0x02c661f1 (LOAD)\n- Written as write at 0x02c66209 (CLEAR)",
