      "name": "ExtractPacketFieldValue",
      "signature": "uint ExtractPacketFieldValue(byte * pPacketData, uint nPacketSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__d2regcall",
      "comment": "Extracts a field value from a binary packet based on message type using lookup tables and jump dispatch.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Validate packet has minimum size (>= 1 byte) and packet type (first byte <= 0xB4)\\n2. Lookup size value in table (DAT_02c6a900) using packet type as index\\n3. If size value is zero, return zero (invalid packet type)\\n4. If size value is non-negative (fixed-size packet), store size and return\\n5. If size value is negative (variable-size packet):\\n   a. Calculate offset into jump table (packet_type - 0x16)\\n   b. Validate offset is within bounds (0-0x9D)\\n   c. Load handler address from jump table at (DAT_02c66934 + offset*4)\\n   d. Dispatch to type-specific handler\\n6. Each handler extracts field from specific packet offset and validates packet size:\\n   - Type 0x16 (13 bytes): Extract WORD at +1\\n   - Type 0x26 (variable): Extract two null-terminated strings at +10\\n   - Type 0x3E (2 bytes): Extract BYTE at +1\\n   - Type 0x5B (34 bytes): Extract WORD at +1\\n   - Type 0x94 (9 bytes): Extract BYTE at +1, calculate (value+2)*3\\n   - Type 0x9C-0x9D (3 bytes): Extract BYTE at +2\\n   - Type 0xA6 (4 bytes): Extract WORD at +2\\n   - Type 0xA8-0xAA (7 bytes): Extract BYTE at +6\\n   - Type 0xAC (13 bytes): Extract BYTE at +12\\n   - Type 0xAE (4 bytes): Extract WORD at +1, cap at 0x1FD, add 3\\n   - Type 0xAF (2 bytes): Extract BYTE at +1, return 2 if zero else value+1\\n   - Type 0xB3 (8 bytes): Extract BYTE at +1, add 8\\n7. If packet is too small for field extraction, return zero\\n8. Store extracted value in output parameter and return\\n\\nParameters:\\n- pPacketData: Pointer to packet buffer (first byte = message type ID)\\n- nPacketSize: Size of packet in bytes\\n- pFieldValue: Pointer to output DWORD for extracted field value\\n\\nReturns:\\n- Extracted field value (varies by packet type)\\n- 0 if packet is invalid, wrong type, or too small\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Type 0x26 requires two variable-length null-terminated strings\\n- Type 0xAE caps input value at 0x1FD before adding offset\\n- Type 0xAF returns constant 2 if flag byte at +1 is zero\\n- Invalid packet types return 0\\n- Insufficient packet size for field extraction returns 0\\\"",
