      "name": "GetSocketAddressAsString",
      "signature": "void GetSocketAddressAsString(void * this, char * pOutputBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "comment": "Retrieves the local socket address and converts it to a dotted-decimal IP address string.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate and zero-initialize local buffer variables for socket address structure and output buffer\n2. Set address length parameter to sizeof(sockaddr) (0x10 = 16 bytes)\n3. Call getsockname() to retrieve the local address bound to the socket handle\n4. Convert the retrieved binary socket address to ASCII dotted-decimal format using inet_ntoa()\n5. Copy the resulting IP address string to output buffer using CopyMemoryWithAlignment()\n\nParameters:\n  pOutputBuffer (char*): Output buffer that receives the socket's local IP address as a null-terminated string\n\nReturns:\n  void: IP address string written to pOutputBuffer; caller must ensure buffer is large enough\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - getsockname() failure will result in zero-initialized address (0.0.0.0)\n  - inet_ntoa() converts in_addr structure to dotted-decimal format\n  - CopyMemoryWithAlignment() copies with 0x7fffffff max length (entire string)\n  - DAT_02c6b248 contains the socket handle used for address retrieval\n\nStructure Layout - sockaddr (16 bytes):\n  Offset  Size  Field          Type       Description\n  0x00    2     sa_family      ushort     Address family (AF_INET for IPv4)\n  0x02    14    sa_data[14]    byte[14]   Family-specific address data",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:cf0ed8aa79a88bb88ab7c8ce7e21838f",
