      "name": "GetLibraryInitializationMode",
      "signature": "uint GetLibraryInitializationMode(int param1)",
      "calling_convention": "__d2regcall",
      "comment": "Retrieves the thread-safe initialization mode of the library.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load g_bLibraryInitialized flag from address 0x02c6b418\n2. Check if library is fully initialized (value 1 or 2) - return 1 if true\n3. If not initialized, check alternate initialization flag at 0x02c6b244\n4. If alternate flag is 0, return 0 (initialization not started)\n5. If alternate flag is non-zero, enter critical section with validation\n6. Load g_nThreadInitMode from address 0x02c6b420\n7. Leave critical section and return the thread initialization mode\n\nReturns:\n  0 - Library initialization not yet started (g_bLibraryInitialized_alt is 0)\n  1 - Library is fully initialized (g_bLibraryInitialized is 1 or 2)\n  Other - Thread-specific initialization mode from g_nThreadInitMode\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  This function uses __stdcall convention with callee cleanup.\n  The critical section lock is only acquired when querying thread init mode.\n  Double-checked locking pattern: check flag without lock, then acquire lock only if needed.",
