      "name": "DequeueMessage",
      "signature": "uint DequeueMessage(void * pDestBuffer, int param2)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Dequeues a message from the thread-safe message queue.\n\nThis function is a wrapper around DequeueMessageWithTimestamp that acquires the critical section lock, validates message timestamps if the library is initialized, copies message data to the destination buffer, and updates the queue head pointer before releasing the lock.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Pass destination buffer pointer to DequeueMessageWithTimestamp\n2. Critical section is acquired by the callee (thread-safe synchronization)\n3. Message is validated for timestamp freshness (within 500ms threshold)\n4. Message data (up to 516 bytes) is copied to destination buffer\n5. Message ID is extracted from message node offset +0x204\n6. Queue head pointer is updated to next node (offset +0x20c)\n7. Notification event is sent via Ordinal_10043(0x46, 0)\n8. Critical section lock is released and return value is passed back\n\nParameters:\n- pDestBuffer: Pointer to destination buffer for message data (capacity: 516 bytes max)\n\nReturns:\n- Message ID on successful dequeue\n- 0xFFFFFFFF (-1) on failure (empty queue or stale message timestamp)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Message copy size is clamped to maximum of 516 bytes (0x204)\n- Timestamp validation only occurs when library is initialized (g_bLibraryInitialized == 2)\n- Empty queue returns -1 without error\n- Stale messages (older than 500ms) are rejected with -1\n\nStructure Layout (Message Node):\nOffset | Size | Field Name    | Type      | Description\n-------|------|---------------|-----------|------------------------------\n+0x000 | 516  | messageData   | byte[516] | Message payload data\n+0x204 | 4    | messageId     | uint      | Message identifier\n+0x208 | 4    | timestamp     | DWORD     | Tick count when enqueued\n+0x20c | 4    | pNextNode     | void*     | Pointer to next message node\nTotal: 528 bytes (0x210)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:50efb6c37a868379ce8439bd65fe6d05",
