      "name": "InitializeLibraryResources",
      "signature": "void * InitializeLibraryResources(int nInitMode, void * pThreadParam, int nParam3, int nParam4)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes library resource pool and conditionally creates worker thread for network processing\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear global initialization state flags at 0x02c6b3fc and 0x02c6b3f4  \n2. Initialize critical section at g_CriticalSection for thread synchronization\n3. Allocate 0xc2 bytes (194 bytes) via AllocateMemoryWithTracking for resource pool\n4. Zero-fill allocated pool using REP STOSD for 0x1ef dwords (1260 bytes total)\n5. Store nInitMode parameter to global library state at g_bLibraryInitialized\n6. Branch on nInitMode value:\n   - Mode 1 or 2: Call ProcessNetworkPacket with encoded parameter (0xaf encoding)  \n   - Other modes: Create worker thread via CreateThread pointing to InitializeNetworkConnection\n7. Store thread handle at global 0x02c6b3f8 and thread ID at 0x02c6b240\n8. Return thread handle for worker modes or 0x1 for direct initialization modes\n\nParameters:\n  nInitMode (int): Initialization mode determining execution path\n    - 1 or 2: Direct initialization via ProcessNetworkPacket call\n    - Other values: Worker thread creation mode\n  pThreadParam (void *): Context parameter passed to worker thread routine\n  nParam3 (int): Additional parameter (purpose unclear from current analysis)  \n  nParam4 (int): Additional parameter (purpose unclear from current analysis)\n\nReturns:\n  void *: Thread handle (HANDLE cast) if worker thread created, 0x1 for direct init modes\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Resource pool allocation tracked via AllocateMemoryWithTracking with unknown tracking data\n  - Zero-fill uses EDI/ECX registers with REP STOSD for performance\n  - ProcessNetworkPacket encoding: CONCAT22 creates 0xaf XX word from nInitMode\n  - Thread routine entry point: InitializeNetworkConnection at unknown address\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0xc2 (194): Size of allocated resource pool in bytes\n  0x1ef (495): DWORD count for zero-fill operation (1980 bytes)  \n  0xaf (175): Encoding byte for ProcessNetworkPacket parameter\n  0x1: Return value for direct initialization modes\n  \nGlobal Memory Layout:\n  0x02c6b3fc: Initialization state flag (cleared on entry)\n  0x02c6b3f4: Secondary state flag (cleared on entry)  \n  0x02c6b244: Pointer to allocated resource pool\n  0x02c6b3f8: Storage for created thread handle\n  0x02c6b240: Storage for thread ID from CreateThread\n  g_bLibraryInitialized: Library mode flag storage\n  g_CriticalSection: Critical section for synchronization\n\nError Handling:\n  No explicit error checking visible for memory allocation or thread creation\n  Relies on called functions (AllocateMemoryWithTracking, CreateThread) for error handling",
